title: Sparc_PostSorting
---
<<SetNarrator GameManager $Sparc Default>>
{$Sparc}: Great work sorting out that trash! Now we just need to take that trash and process it! 
    ->How do I do that?
<<SetNarrator GameManager $Sparc Delight>>
{$Sparc}: : It's easy! Walk up to the yellow bin and take out a piece of trash!
<<ForcedOutlineEnd SparcNPC>>
===

title: Sparc_MachineExplain
---
<<SetNarrator GameManager $Sparc Displease>>
{$Sparc}: When there were people on the island, the machines here used to help them make the island a better place...
<<SetNarrator GameManager $Sparc Delight>>
{$Sparc}: But now that you're here, we can get started again!
<<SetNarrator GameManager $Sparc Default>>
{$Sparc}: *bzzt* As you can see, there are many different types of machines here, each with their own use. 
{$Sparc}: Each piece of trash needs to be processed by several machines before it can be recycled.
===

title: TrashChoose0
---
{$Sparc}: Let's see what trash you grabbed out!
-> *Show {$Sparc} your junk*
{$Sparc}: Ahh! You got some {$SelectedTrash} Material! I'll run you over the basics.
<<jump TrashTypeDetection>>
===

title: AluminiumExplain
---
S.P.A.R.C: Aluminium cans need to be processed in the shredder. *beep!*. Go ahead and put it into the shredder! Watch your fingers!
    -> *Put the can into the shredder*
S.P.A.R.C: Now that you've shredded it, you need to clean it!
    -> *Take out can and put into washer*
//Washer progress bar
//if washer is done:

S.P.A.R.C: Lastly, you can put the cleaned aluminium into the smelter. *bzzt*
    -> *Put the cleaned aluminium into smelter*
S.P.A.R.C: This will smelt it down into crude aluminium that you can use to craft with!
<<set $HoldingItem = false>>
//<<jump TrashChoose1>>
===
title: CardboardExplain
---
S.P.A.R.C: *beep!* Cardboard and Paper trash needs to be washed first! Washing any trash item will always take 5 seconds, regardless of their material.
    -> *Put cardboard in washer*
S.P.A.R.C: Now we need to smelt it. Let's pop it in for 5 seconds.
    -> *Put cardboard in smelter*
S.P.A.R.C: Last step is to use the roller! This should create paper scraps that we can use! *bzzzt!*
    -> *Use the roller on the paper*
S.P.A.R.C: Great work!

<<set $HoldingItem = false>>
//<<jump TrashChoose1>>
===
title: GlassExplain
---
S.P.A.R.C: Glass items such as bottles and jars need to be processed in the crusher. *beep!*

    -> *Put the glass item into the shredder*

S.P.A.R.C: Now that you've crushed it, you need to clean it!

    -> *Take out glass and put into washer*

//Washer progress bar
//if washer is done:

S.P.A.R.C: Now all you need to do is put the cleaned glass into the smelter. Glass smelts into 
Foggy Glass!

<<set $HoldingItem = false>>
//<<jump TrashChoose1>>
===
title: PlasicExplain
---
S.P.A.R.C: Plastic items like containers and lids need to go into the shredder.
    -> *Put plastic into the shredder*
S.P.A.R.C: *beep* Now you'll need to clean them. 
    -> *Take out plastic container and put into washer*
//Washer progress bar
//if washer is done:
S.P.A.R.C: Great work! Now put the cleaned plastic into the smelter!
    -> *Put the cleaned plastic into the smelter*
 S.P.A.R.C: *bzzt* This will smelt it down into Re-pearl that you can use to craft items!

<<set $HoldingItem = false>>
//<<jump TrashChoose1>>
===


title: TrashChoose1
---
<<if visited_count("TrashChoose1") > 3>>
// jump Paulie_EndRecycle
<<else>>
    {$Sparc}: Let's see what you grabbed this time!
    -> *Show {$Sparc} the {$SelectedTrash} trash you grabbed*
    <<jump TrashTypeDetection>>  
<<endif>>
===


title: TrashTypeDetection
---
<<if visited ("SelectedAluminium") == true && visited ("AluminiumExplain") == false>>
    <<jump AluminiumExplain>>
<<elseif visited ("SelectedOrganic") == true && visited ("CardboardExplain") == false>>
    <<jump CardboardExplain>>
<<elseif visited ("SelectedGlass") == true && visited ("GlassExplain") == false>>
    <<jump GlassExplain>>
<<elseif visited ("SelectedPlastic") == true&& visited ("PlasicExplain") == false>>
    <<jump PlasicExplain>>
<<endif>>
===